<title>UK: Ivory coast seeks higher cocoa price.</title>
<headline>Ivory coast seeks higher cocoa price.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ivory Coast Commodities Minister Guy Alain Gauze said he will go to Brazil at the end of June for talks about how to improve cocoa prices.</p>
<p>&quot;We are thinking about what to do to improve more cocoa prices,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The prices are good but we are looking to improve them,&quot; he added.  </p>
<p>When asked if he would consider holding back cocoa sales Gauze said &quot;This is something we are thinking about.&quot;</p>
<p>Gauze said he still expects a world cocoa deficit this year.</p>
<p>He was talking to Reuters on the periphery of a meeting of the Association of Coffee Producing Countries.</p>
<p>In February Gauze had said that the Ivory Coast would only market its midcrop cocoa if prices were right.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
